t('20 · How the sixteen modules connect',p('A line in an architecture diagram must mean something precise. The paths below distinguish the running synthetic application, separately executable research libraries and inactive operational integration. “Engineering complete” does not make every path active.')+lanes('Figure T15. Current connections and boundaries across N01–N16.',[('N01 authentication + source checks','All authorized API / crew reads','active'),('N09 simulator → observations','N02 monitor → SQLite → N03 UI','active'),('N04 visual language','N03 browser + N05 renderer','active'),('N05 region selection → N06 mapping','Authorized crew data / N02 read state','active'),('N08 synthetic archive','N06 waveform lookup / replay UI','active'),('N10 permitted non-private context','Sleep view / N09 scenario context','active'),('N07 scientific originals','N08/N11/N12 authentic input campaign','inactive'),('N11/N12 saved research evidence','Scoped existing research UI / backup','active'),('N13 pinned original corpus','N14 offline lexical library / CLI','active'),('N14 evidence → N15 research library','Approved factual answer in main app','inactive'),('N16 four-tool recorded coordinator','Operational dispatch / N02 authority','inactive')])+h('Read the boundaries correctly')+p('N07 has local-source engineering, but authentic-data suitability and missing-source requirements still block broad downstream validation. N13→N14 lexical research is real offline code; it is not the app’s older Research Library route. N15 can perform non-native source reproduction or governed abstention, but unreviewed factual rules and current native execution remain inactive. N16 has a recorded synthetic coordinator; the app’s case template is a different implementation.')+p('N01 privacy and N02 alert authority apply across the active application. N06 may read existing N02 evidence, never independently create/acknowledge alerts. N12 forecasts do not become operational risk decisions, and N11’s rejected forest cannot silently replace the rule detector.')+refs('services/api/server.mjs','services/api/engine.mjs','packages/anatomy-link.mjs','services/research-answer/governed-service.mjs','services/agent/master-contract.mjs','docs/MODULE_TRACKER.md'),'compact','ch20')
t('21 · APIs, HTTP and local networking',p('An <strong>API</strong> is a contract for program requests. <strong>HTTP</strong> carries those requests; REST-style routes identify resources and use verbs such as GET (read) and POST (submit an action). <strong>JSON</strong> represents objects and lists as readable text. <strong>localhost</strong> means your own machine; <strong>http://127.0.0.1:3000</strong> selects its local ASTRA server on port 3000.')+p('ASTRA serves static browser files and API routes from the same origin. The frontend therefore does not need a second cloud endpoint or a separate React dev server. Most authenticated reads use the existing cookie; they are not publicly authorized simply because the URL is local.')+table(['Actual route / operation','Contract and important boundary'],[['GET /v1/health','Health/readiness information; a successful HTTP reply and monitoring readiness are separate facts.'],['POST /v1/auth/demo; GET /v1/auth/me','Create permitted demo role session; inspect current identity. POST /v1/auth/logout ends it.'],['GET /v1/crew/CREW-03','Crew-scoped projection; telemetry/predictions/checkins/sleep-sessions subroutes have their own handling.'],['GET /v1/crew/CREW-03/anatomy','Allowlisted region and bounded source/cutoff query; read-only linked panel.'],['GET /v1/crew/CREW-03/waveforms','Permitted recording catalog; recording/chunks/channel subroutes preserve source identity. POST /v1/ingest/waveforms is role-controlled.'],['GET /v1/scenarios / runs','Read presets and eligible versioned run/context/replay state.'],['POST /v1/scenarios/{id}/start|step|pause|resume|stop|reset','Authorized command with run/revision/request identity validation; not arbitrary scenario code.'],['GET /v1/n10/crew/CREW-03','Consent/actor/scope-controlled personal context; /records handles allowed record intake.'],['GET /v1/comms/queue; POST /v1/comms/control','Inspect durable report delivery; privileged synthetic configuration is distinct from receipt.'],['GET /v1/provenance; GET /v1/audit','Source context and role-scoped audit views. No general arbitrary SQL interface.'],['POST /v1/ingest/telemetry','Optional service-authenticated scalar producer; unset ingest token disables it.']],[48,52])+h('A source-grounded request example')+code('GET /v1/crew/CREW-03/anatomy?region=cardiovascular\n\nResponse fields include:\n{ "schema_version": "astra.n06.link.v1",\n  "synthetic": true, "clinical_validation": false,\n  "crew_id": "CREW-03", "as_of": "[source cutoff]", ... }')+p('This is an abbreviated field example, not a fresh response with invented observations. Errors distinguish 401 unauthenticated, 403 forbidden, 409 conflict and 422 invalid input; unavailable functions can use 503. The exact error code and reason should be shown rather than translated into a successful medical answer.')+refs('services/api/server.mjs → route branches','services/api/anatomy.mjs','packages/contracts.mjs → AppError'),'compact','ch21')
t('21 · Configuration and API-key truth',p('The supported presentation is local. No mandatory remote AI or NASA API key is found in the actual startup path. A model file’s presence is different from authorization to load it. Configure only environment variables that the code really reads; do not invent OPENAI_API_KEY, NASA_API_KEY or a Supabase setup for this demo.')+table(['Service / feature','Local / cloud; key; status; source'],[['Main frontend and backend','Local; no API key. HOST=127.0.0.1, PORT=3000. One Node HTTP process. services/api/server.mjs.'],['SQLite persistence','Local file; no database login. ASTRA_DB chooses file; default data/runtime/astra.sqlite. services/api/store.mjs.'],['Synthetic mission clock','Local generator; no key. ASTRA_SPEED default 30, permitted 1–3600; use 1 for presentation. services/api/server.mjs.'],['Demo identities','Local role sessions; no external identity credential. ASTRA_DEMO defaults enabled unless false. Not a production login provider.'],['External scalar telemetry producer','Local service contract; optional ASTRA_INGEST_TOKEN. Missing token → INGEST_DISABLED, not anonymous ingestion. services/api/auth.mjs.'],['OpenAI / Qwen cloud / Supabase','Not required; no enabled dependency established in the supported demo. Missing those cloud credentials has no effect on this path.'],['NASA / Hugging Face','No runtime key needed for retained publications/model assets. Historical public acquisition code is separate and is not executed by npm start.'],['N14 MiniLM embeddings','Local ONNX research runtime; no remote model API key. Fresh inference permission absent; lexical remains available. encoder.mjs.'],['N15 Qwen','Local GGUF / llama.cpp; no remote AI key. Native startup/resource authorization absent; current answering support remains restricted. model-admission.mjs.'],['N16 tool workers','Local synthetic SQL source; no cloud key. Separate sealed-source/startup permissions required; operational integration inactive. master-contract.mjs.']],[31,69])+h('Where settings belong')+p('Set variables in PowerShell’s <code>$env:NAME</code> or WSL’s <code>export NAME=value</code> before launching. The current CLI readers do not establish an automatic .env-file loader. Do not paste secrets into a source file. A service token should be treated as a secret if that optional producer is separately configured; no real token is printed here.')+h('Offline does not mean already installed')+p('With local dependencies/assets present, the verified demo does not need internet. A fresh machine missing Node, npm packages, GLBs, vendor files or scientific sources cannot conjure them offline. Recover the approved local installation rather than allowing hidden model/dataset downloads. Binding to loopback and preserving the selected database remain essential.')+refs('services/api/server.mjs → HOST/PORT/ASTRA_DB/ASTRA_SPEED/ASTRA_DEMO/ASTRA_INGEST_TOKEN','services/api/auth.mjs','services/research-retrieval/encoder.mjs','services/research-answer/model-admission.mjs'),'compact')
t('22 · Tests, performance and evidence',p('A unit test checks a small function; an integration test checks components together; an end-to-end test follows a real workflow. A DOM harness can verify browser logic quickly but is not real graphics/browser acceptance. Regression tests repeat relevant checks after a fix. A passing synthetic test cannot establish clinical safety.')+h('Latest retained presentation qualification · 9 Nov 2026')+table(['Evidence','Observed result / interpretation'],[['Automated QA / syntax','258 distinct passes, 0 failures, 0 skips; 297 JavaScript syntax/import checks. Overlapping later UI reruns are not extra distinct tests.'],['Actual Chrome 156.0.8078.80','14/14 workflow groups at 1× and 14/14 at native 200% zoom; eight viewport/zoom audits and 120 native Tab interactions.'],['Startup / API','Windows CLI ≈0.71 s; WSL ≈0.78 s. Health API p95 ≈14.7 ms from eight samples.'],['Crew / anatomy panel','Crew switch with 3D remount ≈8.22–8.88 s. Native region-to-completed-panel p95 ≈715.5 ms, including browser-driver waits.'],['Scenario / waveform','Start + manual 300 s advance ≈1.42 s. Import ≈389 ms; playback observation ≈901 ms.'],['Recovery','Recovered browser panel ≈8.37 s; producer paused for same committed-count verification, no new N12 job.'],['Sampled memory / temporary storage','Browser JS heap ≈36.3 MiB; parent Node RSS ≈230.2 MiB; temporary SQLite ≈24.1 MiB, removed. Not peak or GPU guarantees.'],['Graphics cleanup','Retained counters returned to zero live contexts/buffers/programs/textures and pending callbacks after navigation.'],['Backup video','Successful silent 1280×720 capture at 2 fps, about 823 KB. Historical capture predates the final compact CSS-only Logout repair.']],[34,66])+h('What p95 means')+p('A p95 is a value below which roughly 95% of the sampled timings fall. It depends on workload, sample count, machine and measurement boundary. An eight-sample API statistic is useful for the recorded local run, not a universal service-level guarantee. JavaScript heap is not total browser/GPU memory.')+h('What was fixed, and what was not proven')+p('Final presentation repaired waveform-import cutoff visibility, stale scenario-command revisions and compact Logout layout. Retained source/status pins account for intentional changes. AC-20 remains unverified: DOM/rAF timing does not measure physically presented frames on designated hardware. This PDF mission inspects retained evidence and newly validates PDF files only; it does not claim a new application, clinical or native-model campaign.')+refs('artifacts/presentation-readiness-20261109/final-validation.json','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md','tests/','scripts/browser-acceptance.mjs','docs/N03_AC20_PHYSICAL_ACCEPTANCE.md'),'compact','ch22')
t('23 · Complete does not mean released',p('This is the current N01–N16 status, using the latest records rather than older historical rows. Formal module closure is stricter than passing a scoped synthetic engineering campaign. INACTIVE describes a feature/interface, not a replacement for a module’s formal status.')+table(['Module','Formal status','Engineering / remaining boundary'],[['N01 Security/privacy','Complete','Local permissions/integrity; not clinical certification.'],['N02 Monitoring','Complete','Deterministic monitoring and durable human-review workflow.'],['N03 Frontend foundation','Partial','Engineering complete; AC-20 physical presented-frame acceptance open.'],['N04 Cinematic UI','Complete','Accepted visual/interaction scope.'],['N05 Anatomy renderer','In Progress','4/4 engineering portions; independent anatomy fidelity, hardware and release gates.'],['N06 Anatomy linkage','In Progress','9/9 synthetic engineering; 8/9 original acceptance, physical gate still open.'],['N07 Scientific sources','In Progress','Local engineering; 7/16 rows; source/suitability gates.'],['N08 Waveform ingest','In Progress','Synthetic engineering complete; authentic-source/full twin/review requirements open.'],['N09 Simulator','In Progress','10/10 synthetic engineering; full scientific/transitive/release gates.'],['N10 Sleep/cognition','In Progress','Synthetic engineering complete; source/privacy-science/prerequisite gates.'],['N11 Anomaly research','In Progress','Engineering complete; forest rejected, no candidate promotion.'],['N12 Forecast research','In Progress','Engineering complete; four synthetic-qualified variants, 12 rejected, zero operational promotion.'],['N13 NASA corpus','In Progress','Local engineering complete; 40 seen/provisional questions, 0 independent approvals.'],['N14 Retrieval','In Progress','Lexical engineering complete; semantic parity unverified, hybrid experimental, native/app gates.'],['N15 Generative research','In Progress','Authorized non-native engineering complete; native startup, positive-support and app gates.'],['N16 Health Agent','In Progress','Four-tool synthetic engineering; operational dispatch/sealed workers inactive.']],[30,18,52])+box('<strong>Open gates:</strong> physical AC-20, anatomy/scientific/clinical review, missing approved sources, prospective questions, embedding parity, native resource permissions, operational integration and release. Synthetic tests or PDFs cannot close them.')+p('The honest claim is a <strong>research prototype with a verified synthetic presentation workflow</strong>, not clinical or flight readiness. Older blocked/unstarted records remain history; use the latest scoped status.')+refs('docs/MODULE_TRACKER.md','docs/MASTER_PLAN.md','docs/CORE_AI_PRIORITY.md','docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md','docs/N05_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md','docs/N06_FINAL_ENGINEERING_COMPLETION.md'),'compact','ch23')
t('24 · Real-world value and future work',p('Space missions may face communication delays, limited bandwidth and periods without immediate ground assistance. A local tool that preserves observations, shows quality, supports human review and makes evidence available offline could be useful in that setting. The current prototype explores those engineering needs; it does not prove suitability for an actual mission.')+h('What the implemented prototype contributes')+ul('A reproducible synthetic scenario can demonstrate exactly how an observation becomes a persisted review event, rather than an unexplained colored card.','Source and knowledge timestamps let replay distinguish an earlier event from information learned later.','Crew-bound anatomy offers navigation into permitted data without pretending to localize disease.','Offline quotations, explicit abstention and separate model-promotion gates keep attribution distinct from unsupported conclusions.','Durable transactions, idempotent commands and cold recovery make demonstrations inspectable after interruption.')+h('What must happen before real sensor or clinical use')+table(['Future work — not delivered by this PDF mission','Why it matters'],[['Acquire approved authentic datasets and device interfaces','Define source rights, consent, calibration, units, cadence, quality and clock behavior before interpreting readings.'],['Independent expert/source/annotation review','Check anatomical fidelity, evidence applicability, reference windows and question labels without the developer impersonating a reviewer.'],['Prospective model evaluation and parity','Use independent data and reference implementations; do not promote from questions or scenarios used during tuning.'],['Hardware and operational qualification','Measure designated physical display performance, resource bounds, secure identities and failure behavior in the intended environment.'],['Clinical and human-factors evaluation','Test benefits, harms, workflow comprehension, false alarms, privacy and medical oversight.'],['Release and mission governance','Obtain explicit deployment approval, appropriate safety/regulatory assessment and operating procedures.']],[56,44])+h('Other possible settings')+p('Remote field stations and ships suggest analogous research directions, not demonstrated deployments. Human oversight remains essential for sensor checks, alert review, scientific applicability and any clinical action.')+box('<strong>Recommended next milestone:</strong> close the independently owned validation gates in order—especially physical AC-20, anatomy fidelity and source/review eligibility—before expanding operational AI. That is a proposed roadmap, not authorization to begin it now.')+refs('research/ASTRA_Deep_Research.md','docs/CORE_AI_PRIORITY.md','docs/MODULE_TRACKER.md','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md'),'compact','ch24')
QA=[
('What problem does ASTRA solve?','It explores offline crew-health review when ground support is delayed.','Local observations, deterministic monitoring, replay and evidence tools support a human workflow.','A clinically certified or deployed space medical system.'),
('How is it different from a normal dashboard?','It connects repeatable scenarios, durable alerts, anatomy navigation and evidence boundaries.','Source/knowledge time, human acknowledgement and cold recovery are inspectable end to end.','That every research component is operationally connected.'),
('Is the health data real or fake?','The displayed crew data are synthetic; real research originals are archived separately.','Simulation commits genuine application records, while BIDMC numerics and NASA texts have separate provenance.','Real astronaut measurements or clinical validation from synthetic runs.'),
('Where do the six astronauts’ readings come from?','A seeded local simulator for six fictional people.','Crew-specific references, noise, time and scenario effects generate the observations.','Connected wearable devices that the repository does not establish.'),
('How does the simulator generate data?','Versioned deterministic code combines authored references and scenario effects.','A seed enables repeatability; cadence, source time and quality are recorded with the run.','A learned physiological digital twin.'),
('What happens when a reading changes?','Eligible changes pass through fixed monitoring rules.','Source-time persistence can create a durable N02 event, update the UI and prepare a template case.','Every unusual number is disease or an emergency.'),
('How does ASTRA detect an emergency?','It demonstrates deterministic review/escalation events, not verified emergency diagnosis.','N02 uses personal-baseline deviations, quality and persistence; human review remains required.','Clinical emergency sensitivity or guaranteed all-clear decisions.'),
('Is detection AI-based or rule-based?','The active N02 detector is rule-based.','Fixed Tier A rules are separate from N11’s shadow model evaluations and N15 text generation.','Qwen or Isolation Forest is deciding live alerts.'),
('Which AI models are actually used?','Different research paths contain forest, forecasting, MiniLM and Qwen implementations.','Lexical search and active monitoring are deterministic; native research permissions and promotion are separate.','That all model assets run on npm start.'),
('Why was Isolation Forest rejected?','It failed the authored detection controls.','Retained results show 0 true positives / 4 false negatives plus 44 seen robustness false episodes.','Successful anomaly detection or improved outcomes from that rejected model.'),
('How does forecasting work?','Persistence repeats a value; OLS fits a line; Theil–Sen uses a median slope.','The full N12 protocol also checks chronological history, calibration and supported horizons.','That a plotted line guarantees a future reading.'),
('Are predictions medically reliable?','Not established. Qualification is synthetic engineering only.','Four registry cells qualify within that scope; twelve are rejected and operational promotions are zero.','Clinical accuracy or universal 90% interval coverage.'),
('Can ASTRA run offline?','Yes, the supported local demo can, with its dependencies and assets already present.','Node serves the frontend/API; SQLite and retained evidence are local.','That missing models/assets will download offline or all cloud-era data are available.'),
('Does it need an API key?','No remote API key is required for the current demo.','Local Qwen would not need a cloud key, but current native execution still needs valid authority.','A mandatory OpenAI, NASA, Supabase or cloud-Qwen account.'),
('Where is the database?','At the path selected by ASTRA_DB.','The CLI default is data/runtime/astra.sqlite; the safe demo uses a fresh temp file and reuses it on recovery.','That artifacts/ is the one live database or sealed fixtures may be reused.'),
('Why SQLite?','It gives local transactional storage without a separate server.','WAL, constraints, append-only histories and request identities support durable prototype behavior.','Automatic encryption, medical certification or mission-grade high availability.'),
('How does anatomy connect with readings?','An allowlisted region maps to permitted crew metrics.','N06 validates crew, source and cutoff, then reads observations and existing N02/N08/N09 context.','An inferred organ-specific disease map.'),
('Does anatomical highlighting diagnose disease?','No. It selects an information context.','The licensed generic mesh is not a personal scan; HR/RR timing is illustrative and quality-gated.','Heart disease from an elevated heart-rate observation.'),
('How are citations verified?','The source, window and exact quoted text are checked.','Hashes and IDs bind the quote to the original publication/version/page span.','That exact attribution proves relevance, entailment or applicability.'),
('How do you prevent hallucinations?','Bound sources, separate support checks and abstain when evidence is insufficient.','Prompt text is untrusted data; invented references and unreviewed positive rules cannot pass the governed path.','That an LLM is hallucination-free or a measured general rate exists.'),
('What does Qwen currently do?','It is a local generation research model, not an active medical answerer in the app.','Historical native runs exist; recent checks verified assets with zero fresh native starts.','Current inference authorization from an old permission or model file.'),
('What does the Health Agent do?','The app shows template cases; a separate prototype demonstrated four SQL tools.','The N16 coordinator reads vitals, quality, baseline and synthetic risk under fixed-source constraints.','A deployed autonomous doctor or a live tool run behind every case page.'),
('Is N16 integrated into the application?','Operational integration remains inactive.','The retained HTML is a recorded standalone trace and does not launch sealed-source workers.','That opening a recorded demo authorizes new worker execution.'),
('How is crew privacy protected?','Session roles, crew scope and feature-specific privacy gates restrict access.','Private cognition also checks consent and actor/device context; audit history is integrity-linked.','That demo login is production identity assurance or admins see all private data.'),
('What is needed for a real wearable?','A validated device adapter plus source, timing, privacy and clinical work.','The scalar ingest contract is a starting boundary, not a completed wearable integration.','Existing live astronaut-device connectivity.'),
('Why could it matter for space missions?','Local review and durable delayed reports may help when immediate ground support is unavailable.','The prototype models communication delay and explicit human acknowledgement.','Demonstrated NASA deployment or flight suitability.'),
('What science supports it?','Authentic NASA publications support research context and source attribution.','N13 retains two originals; source suitability and independent question/support reviews remain open.','NASA endorsement or clinical support for every implemented rule.'),
('What remains unvalidated?','Hardware presentation, anatomy fidelity, authentic-data/model science and operational release.','Native/runtime approvals, independent review, parity and promotion gates are distinct.','That engineering completion closes scientific or clinical gates.'),
('What is the strongest technical contribution?','An inspectable, source-bound synthetic workflow with recovery and honest unavailable states.','Monitoring, anatomy, replay and evidence stay separated by explicit authority and provenance.','A scientifically proven breakthrough beyond the retained results.'),
('What should the next milestone be?','Independent validation before broader operational integration.','Prioritize AC-20, anatomy fidelity, missing approved sources and prospective expert-reviewed evaluation.','That this documentation task starts or authorizes the next campaign.')]
for part in range(3):
 blocks=[]
 for idx,(q,a,tech,no) in enumerate(QA[part*10:(part+1)*10],part*10+1):
  blocks.append(h(str(idx)+' · '+q)+p('<strong>Short answer:</strong> '+a)+p('<strong>Technical:</strong> '+tech)+p('<strong>Do not claim:</strong> '+no))
 t('25 · Judges’ questions '+str(part*10+1)+'–'+str(part*10+10),cols(''.join(blocks[:5]),''.join(blocks[5:]))+refs('Source trails: chapters 5–23 and their referenced implementation files','docs/ASTRA_FINAL_DEMO_READINESS.md','docs/MODULE_TRACKER.md'),'qa compact','ch25' if part==0 else None)
G=[('Frontend','The browser interface a user sees and controls.'),('Backend','The local service that validates, reads, computes and stores results.'),('API','An agreed interface for requests between programs.'),('Database','An organized store of records with defined read/write rules.'),('SQLite','An embedded database engine using local files.'),('JSON','A text format for objects, lists and values.'),('REST','A resource-oriented style of HTTP API design.'),('HTTP','The request/response protocol used by the browser and server.'),('Localhost','Your own machine, commonly addressed as 127.0.0.1.'),('Node.js','The runtime executing ASTRA’s server-side JavaScript.'),('JavaScript','The programming language used across ASTRA’s main implementation.'),('Synthetic data','Intentionally generated data, not measurements from the represented person.'),('Real-world data','Observations collected from an actual source/population, subject to rights and context.'),('Telemetry','Time-stamped measurements transmitted or recorded for monitoring.'),('Sensor','A physical device measuring a property of the world.'),('Waveform','A sequence of signal samples across time.'),('Sampling rate','Samples recorded per second, measured in hertz (Hz).'),('Simulation','Software generation of controlled scenarios or observations.'),('Deterministic','Reproducible output for the same inputs and state.'),('AI','A broad term for computational methods performing intelligent-seeming tasks.'),('Machine learning','Methods that fit patterns from data rather than only fixed rules.'),('LLM','A large language model trained to predict/generate text.'),('Qwen','The model family used in ASTRA’s local text-generation research.'),('Quantization','Reducing numerical weight precision to save model resources.'),('Embeddings','Learned numerical representations of text or other inputs.'),('Retrieval','Finding existing relevant items or text passages.'),('RAG','Retrieval-augmented generation: give retrieved context to a generator.'),('Hallucination','A fluent generated statement not supported by reliable evidence.'),('Anomaly','An unusual pattern relative to a chosen reference.'),('Forecasting','Estimating later values from earlier eligible information.'),('Linear regression','Fitting a line relating input time/features to an outcome.'),('Isolation Forest','Random partition trees scoring how quickly points become isolated.'),('Agent','A system coordinating bounded actions or tools toward a task.'),('Tool calling','Invoking a defined external function with structured arguments.'),('Three.js','A JavaScript library for constructing and rendering 3D scenes.'),('WebGL','A browser graphics interface for accelerated rendering.'),('Mesh','A surface described by vertices and triangles.'),('GLB','A binary glTF container for 3D geometry/material assets.'),('Provenance','The origin, version and transformation history of information.'),('Hash','A content fingerprint useful for detecting changed bytes.'),('Authorization','A decision that a particular actor may perform an action.'),('p95 latency','A timing at/below which about 95% of the sampled requests fall.'),('Scientific validation','Independent evidence that a method is suitable for its claimed use.'),('Abstention','Explicitly withholding an answer when required support is absent.'),('Cold recovery','Restoring committed state in a newly started process.'),('Idempotency','Repeating an identified request without duplicating its committed effect.')]
t('26 · Technical glossary','<div class="gloss">'+''.join(p('<strong>'+e(term)+'.</strong> '+e(defn)) for term,defn in G)+'</div>'+p('<strong>Study path:</strong> User Guide → chapters 2, 5–10 and 20 → research boundaries in 14–19 → judges’ practice in 25. Source inspection: 11 Nov 2026; no application or scientific qualification is claimed by these PDFs.','small')+refs('Repository-relative references throughout this report identify the implementation trail.','ASTRA - Complete User Guide.pdf'),'compact','ch26')
